# Colocated Hook Folders

When a hook grows past ~100 lines or mixes mount lifecycle + per-frame logic + pure helpers, convert it to a folder — do not leave a fat single file.

## Layout

```
hooks/use-example/
  index.ts                 # public barrel only
  use-example.ts           # thin orchestrator
  use-example-*.ts         # private sub-hooks (effects, frame loops)
  *.ts                     # private helpers / types used only here
```

Exemplars: `hooks/use-soldier-locomotion/`, `hooks/use-player-controls/`.

## Placement

| Kind                                                              | Where                                                                                                |
| ----------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Hook-only helpers, types, sub-hooks, finished wiring, mixer mount | **Inside** the hook folder; do **not** re-export from the barrel                                     |
| Pure domain / shared resolution reused by other modules or hooks  | `src/modules/<domain>/utils/` (or a shared hook if it is React lifecycle reused by multiple callers) |

## Barrel

- Export only the public API (`useExample`, diagnostic counters callers need).
- Callers import `@/modules/<domain>/hooks/use-example` (folder), never deep private paths.

## Forbid

- Dumping hook-private helpers into `utils/` “for neatness” when nothing else imports them
- Moving shared resolvers into the hook folder when other features already depend on them
- Re-exporting the whole private surface from `index.ts`
- Splitting for vanity line-count when concerns are still one cohesive unit (see `specs/tech-debt.md`)
